      "recoveryMessages": [
        {
          "role": "user",
          "text": "Write an essay of about 330 words on the history of lighthouses. Plain paragraphs only: no title, headings or lists.",
          "toolUses": 0,
          "toolResults": []
        },
        {
          "role": "assistant",
          "text": "For more than two thousand years, people have built lighthouses to guide sailors past dangerous coasts and into safe harbors. The most famous early example was the Pharos of Alexandria. It was completed around 280 BCE under Ptolemy II and was probably more than one hundred meters tall. At night a fire burned at its summit, and some ancient writers said the light could be seen far out at sea. The Pharos stood for centuries before earthquakes destroyed it, and it was counted among the Seven Wonders of the Ancient World. Its name lives on in the words for lighthouse in several languages, includin",
